{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5495",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the regulation of YAPC through multiple distinct pathways, with the most direct link emerging from its interaction with P2X purinoceptors. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for two different P2X purinoceptor subtypes, P2X 1 and P2X 7, both of which are targeted by a common compound [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This compound is known to target YAPC, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the P2X receptor pathway. The presence of a shared target compound and the distinct targets of Mollicellin N further supports a mechanistic link between the two entities. The evidence is consistent with a role for Mollicellin N in modulating P2X receptor activity, which in turn influences YAPC. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions involved, with the core mechanism centered on the P2X receptor pathway and its downstream effect on YAPC.",
